    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Exceptional 4-Bedroom Bespoke Residence on c.3.2 Acres with Extensive Equestrian Facilities\n\nSet amidst approximately 3.2 acres of beautifully maintained grounds, this outstanding two-storey dormer bungalow offers a rare opportunity to acquire a property that seamlessly combines modern living with exceptional outdoor space and versatility. This property has a traditional character and charm, but being built around 2000, it also offers modern comforts and generous headroom.\n\nThe residence itself is thoughtfully designed, featuring four spacious bedrooms and three well-appointed bathrooms, ideal for family life. Bright and inviting living areas are complemented by a charming conservatory, creating a perfect space to relax while enjoying views of the mature gardens. A generous decking area extends the living space outdoors, ideal for entertaining and al fresco dining. The kitchen and conservatory offer stunning views across the Bride Valley, as far as West Waterford. \n\nThe grounds are a standout feature of this property, with mature landscaping and established planting enhancing the visual appeal. , A greenhouse for the green-fingered is an added bonus. \n\nThe hayfield has been seeded with a horse hay mix and benefits from a natural stream and pond, while a spring water supply is available for animals—adding to the property's self-sufficiency and appeal. Sustainability is a key benefit, with solar PV panels and battery storage providing energy efficiency, supported by a strong B2 BER rating—qualifying for attractive green mortgage rates.\n\nA comprehensive range of outbuildings further elevates this property, including a barn, stables, machinery shed, and a dedicated store room, all offering excellent functionality and flexibility. A CCTV system offers extra peace of mind. \n\nThe property has two entrances, a driveway leading to the house and a separate entrance for tractors and/or machinery that offers direct access to the field to the rear of the barn. \n\nOf note is the inclusion of an arena, making this property especially appealing to equestrian enthusiasts or those seeking a small holding. The generous acreage, secure fencing, and well-laid-out facilities provide excellent scope for hobby farming or equestrian pursuits. The surrounding countryside offers quiet, scenic routes ideal for horse riding (hacking) and dog walking, further enhancing the lifestyle appeal of this unique property. For those interested in fishing, the property offers easy access to both the River Bride and the River Blackwater. \n\nLocation: \nSituated in the peaceful countryside and within easy reach of the local amenities in Rathcormac (7km), Watergrasshill (10km) and Fermoy (12km) and convenient to the M8 motorway and the city. The property is on the bus route for primary school in Rathcormac and secondary school in Fermoy. \n\nKey Features:\n•Bespoke-designed two-storey residence\n•4 spacious bedrooms & 3 bathrooms\n•Bright conservatory & large decking area\n•Solar PV panels with battery storage\n•Solar panels for hot water supply\n•Electric Car Charger\n•B2 BER rating (eligible for green mortgage rates)\n•c.3.2 acres\n•Mature landscaping & greenhouse\n•Hayfield with horse hay mix, stream & pond\n•Barn, stables, machinery shed & store room\n•Private arena\n•Excellent location for hacking and dog walking\n•Ideal for equestrian use or small holding potential\n\nThis is a truly special property offering space, privacy, and versatility in a highly desirable rural yet accessible location.\n\nAccommodation \nGROUND FLOOR\n\nEntrance Hallway: 1.2 x 2.2\nBathroom: 1.8 x 2.2\nMaster Bedroom: 4.3 x 3\nWalk in Wardrobe: 1.8 x 1.1\nEnsuite: 1.2 x 2.4\nBedroom 2: 4.2 x 2.9\nEnsuite: 1.7 x 2.2\nKitchen: 4.2 x 2.1\nLiving Room: 5.1 x 5.1\nConservatory: 8 x 3\n\nFIRST FLOOR\nBedroom 3: 4.3 x 5\nW.C.: 2 X 1.15\nBedroom 4: 4.2 x 5\nW.C.: 1.5 x 2\nLanding: 5.6 x 5\n\nDisclaimer: The above details are for guidance only and do not form part of any contract. They have been prepared with care but we are not responsible for any inaccuracies. All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permission for use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct but any intending purchaser or tenant should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy himself / herself by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. In the event of any inconsistency between these particulars and the contract of sale, the latter shall prevail. The details are issued on the understanding that all negotiations on any property are conducted through this office."
